  "draftIsFinal": false,
  "summary": "I wrote `src/main.ts`, and it passes `typecheck`. I couldn't run `vite build` or load it in a browser, so I haven't seen it render and haven't checked that the camera orbit works.\n\n- **Island:** a jittered 56×56 grid with one flat-shaded triangle per face, so the terrain looks faceted. Faces are coloured by height and slope: sand, grass, rock. Roughly 24 instanced trees (a trunk and two cones each) and about 14 instanced low-poly rocks sit on it.\n- **Water:** a custom shader on a 320 m grid. It has animated vertex waves and faceted normals from screen-space derivatives. It also has a shallow-to-deep colour gradient, a foam line that follows the island's shore, a sun/moon glint, and a fade into the sky colour at distance. A `waveClock` uniform drives the waves, and the sun direction and colour, sky colour and day factor are updated every frame.\n- **Day/night:** a full cycle takes 20 seconds and starts at 9:00. The sun moves on an arc through `app.atmosphere.setSky`, and the sky includes stars. Sun intensity and colour (warm at dusk), the moon light and the hemisphere ambient light all follow the hour. The ambient light never drops below 0.28, so the scene is not black at night.\n- **Camera:** an orbit camera at about 39 m from the island, above the water, with `interactions.orbit` set to `autoRotate: 0.12`. The island fills about 40% of the view width.\n- **Ready flag:** `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set on the first `onFrame` callback and again after `app.ready()`.\n\n",
